xattr oracle case: dump-empty

Isolates --dump of a file with no xattrs: real lists the attrs and
`continue`s silently, so stdout is empty and rc is 0 (no `# file:`
header for an attr-less file).
If the native port regressed to printing a header anyway, out.txt
would be present instead of absent.

Run shape: cwd=<stage>; real `xattr-helper.py --dump` with the checked-in stdin fed raw (estrip's `--dump < <(echo -n ...)` shape, single path without trailing newline unless the case says otherwise); in.manifest + xattrs are the input tree.
Regenerate with fixtures/helpers/generate-xattr.sh.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  worktree-commit: 73091925f35b01b8814a357c60db98334ee94648
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  uid: 1000, umask: 022 (enforced)
  staging: tmpfs (raw non-UTF-8 names OK: yes)
  xattr-fs: user.* xattrs work on tmpfs
  generator-locale: LANG=C.utf8 (enforced); charmap=UTF-8
  date: 2026-10-09 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
  scrub: <SCRATCH>/<CHECKOUT> in args/stdin/out/stderr/stdout
